 if they're going to start seizing assets  which is what happened in in in sri  lanka before with the port  and that would be very serious would  also be a big boost for china's regional  um strategy of of becoming more  prominent and of increasing its muscle  in the region  talking about the region what about  india one of china's rivals uh sri  lanka's closest neighbor and a big  investor as well yeah i mean there's a  big power play going on between india  and china right now we've seen this in  many in many different areas uh they're  professing closeness at the moment  because they're part of the brics  grouping with brazil and russia that  they're all sort of um that they're  showing this sort of new closeness but  at the back of it there's still a lot of  regional issues between the two um india  has just overtaken china as the most  populous nation in in the world um or is  about to this year um so there's a lot  of competitive competition between the  two um india is not really involved in  the in the belton road uh initiative and  it's um it's basically wants to push its  own interests so i think that um we're  going to see they've they've given a lot  of money to sri lanka a lot of support  um i think we're going to see more of  that and um china is really going to  have to step up if it wants to  to win with this uh you know this cap to  capture sri lanka's hearts and minds  it's going to have to step up its  activities clifford kunin thank you very  much

